<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch09-gradient-optimization" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Gradients, Hessians, and Optimization</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>The differential and gradient from Chapter 7 describe first-order change, and the chain rule from Chapter 8 follows that change along constraints. We now use them to locate extrema. Second derivatives supply a quadratic approximation, while examples distinguish a necessary critical-point test from a conclusion about maxima or minima.</p>
  </introduction>

